{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/981041-format-space-for-hermetics","id":981041,"title":"Format Space for Hermetics!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-03T14:54:15-07:00","id":981041,"title":"Format Space for Hermetics!","content":"So Format Space punches the consensus in the face and resets it to fit the users worldview yes?<br /> <br /> Fluffwise, the Technocracy does a lot of machinery stuff and holograms and AI and science.<br /> <br /> So, the Order of Hermes, the grumpy old granddads of the Traditions. The guys who want to kick everyone back to the dark ages when they were in charge. Seems like they'd be EXACTLY the sort of people desperate and stupid enough to attempt this right?<br /> <br /> So, how does it work? Personally, I think, rather than deploying satellites, and delineating a physical zone. A Hermetic version of this effect would require first finding and binding four spirits of the dominant landmarks of the region. Followed by binding the Zeitgeist of the area (Hopefully with a suitably epic fight.) to the terms the Hermetic sets forth, and thus altering the consensus of the area.<br /> <br /> From there, the Hermetic has a limited window to reinforce the &quot;You're not in kansas anymore&quot; Nature of their new fiefdom to their 'subjects'. Lest the occupants technocratic biases undo their hard won victory.<br /> <br /> Not to mention how this would get you a MAJOR response from the local, and possibly even world wide Technocrat command.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:36:17-07:00","id":981616,"title":"","content":"Zeitgeist is the spirit of an age. It's literally German for &quot;time ghost&quot;. You probably mean genius loci or something similar.<br /> <br /> Format Space is effectively a very 'region'-focused version of the same principles behind creating a Horizon Realm, which can to an extent be applied to real-space. Or forcibly and quickly establishing a Sanctum/Laboratory or Chantry/Construct in a temporary manner.<br /> <br /> Your suggestion seems quite legitimate for a (Spirit-based) version of Format Space, creating a Horizon Realm, or setting up a Chantry in an exceptionally violent manner within the Hermetic Paradigm. Props.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:02:21-07:00","id":981641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quantumboost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/981041-format-space-for-hermetics?p=981616#post981616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Zeitgeist is the spirit of an age. It's literally German for &quot;time ghost&quot;. You probably mean genius loci or something similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's deliberate.<br /> <br /> I used Zeitgeist as they're fighting against the spirit of this age, the age of the technocracy, in order to turn back the clock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T13:03:42-07:00","id":981643,"title":"","content":"Ah, okay then. Makes some sense in that case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T02:18:38-07:00","id":982022,"title":"","content":"Hermetics explode from paradox from all the effected sleepers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T16:48:19-07:00","id":982439,"title":"","content":"Paradox doesn't scale per sleeper disturbed. It's an on/off thing. Are sleepers disturbed? If yes, the paradox is worse. If not? It's not quite so bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T20:00:13-07:00","id":982523,"title":"","content":"It definitely scales by absurdity of the goal. This is a HUGE goal. Formatting usually occurs completely &quot;off camera&quot; in the Umbra to create more Conventional Space or for the ultra-rare un-formated sector in the web. And those are difficult to achieve goals. Reformatting Springfield, IL and making it &quot;ye Olde Fielde o'Waters a-Bournein'&quot; is going to be on the scale of &quot;Godlike&quot; to start with.<br /> <br /> So... high level of Difficulty (as in, &quot;above 10&quot;), massive number of successes, protracted Ritual. The chance for a bad roll increases incrementally with more dice rolled and more times the dice are rolled. The Paradox is additive across all rolls. <br /> <br /> And it doesn't matter how many Sleepers are being disturbed, but taking in a big area and re-writing the source code to the local reality means that each and every Sleeper in the area is a Witness to this act of monumental Hubris.<br /> <br /> So, I stand with Lian. Dark Ages recidivist Hermetic Master go BOOM! He'd be better off going into Conventional Space and trying to recreate the Ptolemaic Spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T01:20:36-07:00","id":982595,"title":"","content":"The additional Paradox from extended rolls matters only in case of a botch...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T13:59:58-07:00","id":982911,"title":"","content":"And the chance of botches increases with additional rolls. And ANY botch activates all the &quot;hanging&quot; Paradox. It's all in the math. <br /> <br /> What the OP describes is pretty much the perfect recipe for a Paradox disaster. Mage go BOOM! <br /> <br /> The upshot is that the Hermetic is likely to get exactly what he is wishing for. The downside of that is that it's going to be a Paradox Realm and he's going to be in a deep Quiet. That is, if he's alive. <br /> <br /> This isn't one of those &quot;the rules don't control for this so we have to make something up to explain why something so easy isn't going on all the time&quot; situation (like making mulch into solid gold). This is something that doesn't happen because the RAW actually address why it's not going on all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T16:07:28-07:00","id":982982,"title":"","content":"The fact that the Technocracy doesn't use it on Earth should be good enough reason for why other groups aren't. Even the Wu Lung Mandate of Heaven trick didn't stay stable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:53:29-07:00","id":983041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/981041-format-space-for-hermetics#post981041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So, the Order of Hermes, the grumpy old granddads of the Traditions. The guys who want to kick everyone back to the dark ages when they were in charge. Seems like they'd be EXACTLY the sort of people desperate and stupid enough to attempt this right?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Stop stop stop stop stop!<br /> <br /> This meme needs to stop. At no point does the Order of Hermes, nor any of the Traditions, ever state that they want to &quot;kick everyone back to the dark ages when they were in charge.&quot; Where you might find that assertion is in the Technocracy books, which are written from their perspective and with their propaganda. However, even in Tradition propaganda, no one wants to blow it all up and subjugate the Sleepers. Hell, the idea what the OoH was in charge of anything is mostly false, as they mostly just kept to themselves, which was actually the problem; they didn't share.<br /> <br /> What the Traditions want is to <i>expand</i> the Consensus, where the Technocracy wants to constrict it. Very few, and none credible, think that all of the &quot;technological&quot; advancements and conveniences need to be taken away. No one wants to turn back the clock. We can have cars and magic carpets, so long as we can convince the Sleepers that it's possible. The real conflict comes down to whether or not it's a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T20:23:30-07:00","id":983113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/981041-format-space-for-hermetics?p=983041#post983041\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Stop stop stop stop stop!<br /> <br /> This meme needs to stop. At no point does the Order of Hermes, nor any of the Traditions, ever state that they want to &quot;kick everyone back to the dark ages when they were in charge.&quot; Where you might find that assertion is in the Technocracy books, which are written from their perspective and with their propaganda. However, even in Tradition propaganda, no one wants to blow it all up and subjugate the Sleepers. Hell, the idea what the OoH was in charge of anything is mostly false, as they mostly just kept to themselves, which was actually the problem; they didn't share.<br /> <br /> What the Traditions want is to <i>expand</i> the Consensus, where the Technocracy wants to constrict it. Very few, and none credible, think that all of the &quot;technological&quot; advancements and conveniences need to be taken away. No one wants to turn back the clock. We can have cars and magic carpets, so long as we can convince the Sleepers that it's possible. The real conflict comes down to whether or not it's a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except when it does. There is no real organization or hierarchy in the Traditions. Sure there are relative levels of power, but, really, no one is giving orders and no one is listening. A few of the Traditions proper kinda sorta have hierarchies. Most don't. You can't make an organization chart with the Council of the Nine at the top and then position everyone else in it... It's all very ad hoc. Just because Master So and so says something, if he's not the head of your Chantry, you can listen to him as much or as little as you want to. To get anything done organizationally takes consensus (little c) building.<br /> <br /> So there is no one true orthodoxy. There's a lot of different objectives than are able to hang loosely together. So there is no overall &quot;Return to the Dark Ages&quot; agenda for the Nine Traditions, but that doesn't mean that some mages don't think exactly that way. And some of them are probably very powerful and influential. And, whatever pie in the sky idealization of &quot;Consensus Expansion&quot; is out there, if it is out there at the level of the Council of Nine, is a mission statement or aspiration than it is a manifesto. Which means it's just another meme too. Sure, there are some mages out there living and dying to try to MAKE THAT HAPPEN. But, then, there are also mages out there trying to strip away all this Technocratic schmutz and restore the world to a more pristine and magic-friendly state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T21:09:43-07:00","id":983130,"title":"","content":"Ok, yes. The Traditions are a disparate bunch with barely aligned end goals, if any of them even have end goals to speak of.<br /> <br /> However, my point still stands. This &quot;The Traditions want to send us screaming back to the Dark Ages,&quot; or in this case just the Order of Hermes, is one that is leveled against them with no nuance, and in staunch support of the Technocratic position. It's fine and well to be a fan of the Technocracy, but this wrong idea that people spread about how the evil Reality Deviants want to destroy all the good that the benevolent Technocracy has done for us does a disservice to the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T23:23:21-07:00","id":983180,"title":"","content":"I don't think that the OoH as a whole wants to turn back the clock, but some mages think \u201cBring back the golden Age\u201c. But keep in mind that their Golden Age has very little in common with the Dark Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T12:02:09-07:00","id":983445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/981041-format-space-for-hermetics?p=983130#post983130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, yes. The Traditions are a disparate bunch with barely aligned end goals, if any of them even have end goals to speak of.<br /> <br /> However, my point still stands. This &quot;The Traditions want to send us screaming back to the Dark Ages,&quot; or in this case just the Order of Hermes, is one that is leveled against them with no nuance, and in staunch support of the Technocratic position. It's fine and well to be a fan of the Technocracy, but this wrong idea that people spread about how the evil Reality Deviants want to destroy all the good that the benevolent Technocracy has done for us does a disservice to the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Umm.... Considering 90% of what was 'bad' about the Dark Ages is only 'bad' from a Technocrat point of view....<br /> <br /> And two, destroying the limited consensus would destroy technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T12:33:43-07:00","id":983455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/981041-format-space-for-hermetics?p=983445#post983445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Umm.... Considering 90% of what was 'bad' about the Dark Ages is only 'bad' from a Technocrat point of view....</div> </div> </div> </div>And for each and every mage whose paradigm and abilities doen't include conjuring toilet paper out of thin air.<br /> <br /> Most mages in the traditions these days grew up in modern society. They are used to nice homes, heating, electricity (or some sort of energy..) and most of them don't just go 'L<i>ol this all sucks lets remove it all</i>'.<br /> Most of them simply want normal sleepers to experience wonder and magic. Not return to some lone towers in ye olde woods yonder, because most masters that even experienced those times are GONE, and if they are not, they get smacked down for ideas like that these days.<br /> <br /> So no. The Dark Ages hold a lot of bad things for most modern mages' views, and even more so, they wouldn't simply be able to emulate all the niceties they had before in modern times. Just because it's in the sphere description doesn't mean the mage can do it, or the paradigm even supports it. I really need to thump this so hard.<br /> <br /> The Traditions today have grown up in modern times, not Dark Ages. They want Technocracy control gone, they want Wonder and Magick to be normal, but they don't want to return to a Westoroth they never lived in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-07-2016, 03:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T12:41:37-07:00","id":983460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/981041-format-space-for-hermetics?p=983455#post983455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And for each and every mage whose paradigm and abilities doen't include conjuring toilet paper out of thin air.<br /> <br /> Most mages in the traditions these days grew up in modern society. They are used to nice homes, heating, electricity (or some sort of energy..) and most of them don't just go 'L<i>ol this all sucks lets remove it all</i>'.<br /> Most of them simply want normal sleepers to experience wonder and magic. Not return to some lone towers in ye olde woods yonder, because most masters that even experienced those times are GONE, and if they are not, they get smacked down for ideas like that these days.<br /> <br /> So no. The Dark Ages hold a lot of bad things for most modern mages' views, and even more so, they wouldn't simply be able to emulate all the niceties they had before in modern times. Just because it's in the sphere description doesn't mean the mage can do it, or the paradigm even supports it I need to thump this so hard.<br /> <br /> The Traditions today have grown up in modern times, not Dark Ages. They want Technocracy control gone, they want Wonder and Magick to be normal, but they don't want to return to Westoroth they never lived in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except... those things are synonomous? One is the other. If the Technocrats control of the peoples minds is gone, the paradigm of reason broken, then technology won't work anymore... That's pretty clearly stated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T12:46:56-07:00","id":983465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/981041-format-space-for-hermetics?p=983460#post983460\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except... those things are synonomous? One is the other. If the Technocrats control of the peoples minds is gone, the paradigm of reason broken, then technology won't work anymore... That's pretty clearly stated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you think in pure black and white, and that there can only be pure mythical magic OR pure technology overlords ruling.<br /> It's actually not stated that there can only be one or the other. It's stated that what the consensus believes in, goes.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to the important point: If you teach sleepers that both Magick and technology can exist..even more so that technology is magick..then you have both. You have your Final Fantasy where Magick and Technology intermingle openly.<br /> <br /> Modern Traditions mostly aren't anti-technology. They are anti-Technocratic-oppression. Most modern Mages USE and <i>live</i> with technology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 10-07-2016, 05:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T14:29:13-07:00","id":983533,"title":"","content":"Except that's not the way it works. TECHNOLOGY works, because it makes sense. It is rigorously tested and follows a set of universal rules that the Technocracy hand down. Because everything is self consistent for the most part there is no &quot;But.... why does it work that way?&quot; moment. Or a &quot;But if this does X, doesn't that mean Y?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because these things are planned for in advance. You can't get the Traditions to agree on <i>anything.</i> And you seriously think they'd be capable of maintaining the systems of science and technology while at the same time introducing magic?<br /> <br /> It just wouldn't work. Even the Technocracy has trouble introducing the more fantastical aspects of Enlightened Science to the Consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T14:44:48-07:00","id":983541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/981041-format-space-for-hermetics?p=983445#post983445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Umm.... Considering 90% of what was 'bad' about the Dark Ages is only 'bad' from a Technocrat point of view....<br /> <br /> And two, destroying the limited consensus would destroy technology.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, it wouldn't. By that logic, Paradox and Disbelief happen because &quot;technology&quot; is the dominant paradigm, but that's not the case. Technology rules and mystical magick falls prey to Paradox because of the Technocratic campaign to convince the Sleepers that magic isn't real. This is what I mean by the opposed philosophies between the Technocracy and the mystical mages: the Technocracy wants to constrict the Paradigm, whereas the mystical mages want to expand it. Fewer beliefs as opposed more. You can have cars and guns along side with flying carpets and magic wands as long as people believe in all of those things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T14:47:58-07:00","id":983544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/981041-format-space-for-hermetics?p=983541#post983541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> No, it wouldn't. By that logic, Paradox and Disbelief happen because &quot;technology&quot; is the dominant paradigm, but that's not the case. Technology rules and mystical magick falls prey to Paradox because of the Technocratic campaign to convince the Sleepers that magic isn't real. This is what I mean by the opposed philosophies between the Technocracy and the mystical mages: the Technocracy wants to constrict the Paradigm, whereas the mystical mages want to expand it. Fewer beliefs as opposed more. You can have cars and guns along side with flying carpets and magic wands as long as people believe in all of those things.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference being joe schmoe on the corner couldn't build a magic carpet. And there's nothing indicating that will change except BY restricting the paradigm. It's not done arbitrarily, it's done because it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T15:13:19-07:00","id":983557,"title":"","content":"Joe schmoe on the corner couldn't build a car either. He's going to need the tools and the parts and the knowledge. Manufacturing is, after all, just a Consensus-accepted way to build Wonders/Devices that everyone can use.<br /> <br /> As far as things working by constricting/expanding the paradigm, that's how reality zones, cults, and consors work. You get a group of people to buy into your worldview and things start getting easier, or even coincidental. However, unless you stipulate that a particular reality zone excludes, or has never included, a particular paradigm, everything should still work as normal. An uncontacted tribe in the Amazon won't know about &quot;technology,&quot; and thus modern devices may break down from Disbelief/Paradox, but a group of people conscripted into a suburban cult have seen &quot;technology&quot; work for their whole lives and have no reason to disbelieve it, and yet they can empower a mage's magick with their <b>expanded</b> belief system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T15:39:12-07:00","id":983570,"title":"","content":"I'd split the difference; magick and technology aren't inherently conflicting in terms of Consensus, but introducing new technology and making it &quot;normal&quot;/not requiring Enlightenment requires a degree of dominance in the Consensus that doesn't allow for magick.<br /> <br /> Part of the reason guns work as a normal part of the universe now (as opposed to being a focus for Enlightened Will or a Wonder) is because everyone believes in them - they know they can kill anyone, anytime. What if the Traditions had a reasonable minority share of the Consensus? Ten percent of the time you shoot a guy, he calls out in Enochian and an archangel pushes the bullet aside. Another ten percent of the time, he does some crazy kung fu shit and hands your bullet back to you. Your faith in guns is going to waver a little bit. That doesn't mean guns become Paradoxical, but the Technocracy is unlikely to get the depleted uranium flechette railgun into the Consensus on schedule.<br /> <br /> I like it because it explains why the Technocracy had to do what they did - sharing Enlightenment with the masses means making your works &quot;normal&quot;, and you can't do that as long as anyone believes in vampires/wizards/dragons, so all that's got to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T16:14:35-07:00","id":983584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/981041-format-space-for-hermetics?p=983570#post983570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd split the difference; magick and technology aren't inherently conflicting in terms of Consensus, but introducing new technology and making it &quot;normal&quot;/not requiring Enlightenment requires a degree of dominance in the Consensus that doesn't allow for magick.<br /> <br /> Part of the reason guns work as a normal part of the universe now (as opposed to being a focus for Enlightened Will or a Wonder) is because everyone believes in them - they know they can kill anyone, anytime. What if the Traditions had a reasonable minority share of the Consensus? Ten percent of the time you shoot a guy, he calls out in Enochian and an archangel pushes the bullet aside. Another ten percent of the time, he does some crazy kung fu shit and hands your bullet back to you. Your faith in guns is going to waver a little bit. That doesn't mean guns become Paradoxical, but the Technocracy is unlikely to get the depleted uranium flechette railgun into the Consensus on schedule.<br /> <br /> I like it because it explains why the Technocracy had to do what they did - sharing Enlightenment with the masses means making your works &quot;normal&quot;, and you can't do that as long as anyone believes in vampires/wizards/dragons, so all that's got to go.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. This explains it much better than I have.<br /> <br /> People believing in other things is literally going to sabotage the framework of belief that technology relies on. Maybe it won't collapse immediately, but it will collapse. You'd end up less with Shadowrun, and more with Nausicaa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T16:36:20-07:00","id":983593,"title":"","content":"No, it's a fundamental misunderstanding of the setting. But if that's the custom setting you want to run, then that's your game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:22:37-07:00","id":983620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/981041-format-space-for-hermetics?p=983593#post983593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, it's a fundamental misunderstanding of the setting. But if that's the custom setting you want to run, then that's your game.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.... it's not. Maybe M20 changed it, but as of revised, that's just the way it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:41:06-07:00","id":983635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/981041-format-space-for-hermetics?p=983455#post983455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Most of them simply want normal sleepers to experience wonder and magic.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Do they? Do they really? The Traditions are emphatically not about Mass Ascension. That's the Union's thing. Ascension is personal to the Traditions.<br /> <br /> And that whole &quot;Let's show the Sleepers the WONDER of magic..&quot; that's just as theoretical a goal as has been previously discussed. That may be a party line. But in practice what do Mage characters actually DO? In most chronicles I've run, played in, read about in the context of Mage in the rules or in the fiction or heard described, the number of games that are about &quot;winning hearts and souls&quot; are in the VAST minority. It's a lot like role-playing running a preschool. You've got to have a GREAT hook to make it interesting at all and an even better one for long term or it's about as interesting as &quot;Mage: the Tax Audit&quot; or &quot;Mage: the Bakery&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1062,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","user":"Ajax","date":". 10-07-2016, 09:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:44:20-07:00","id":983641,"title":"","content":"Even in Revised, that's how it worked. Paradox didn't exist before the Order of Reason got together and started their campaign to win hearts and minds and spread disbelief and doubt in everything that wasn't supported by the Order of Reason. It's specifically called out as a recent phenomena, and it wasn't like there was an absence of primitive technology that didn't work jsut because some of the more mystical arts were still around.<br /> <br /> Paradox is a symptom of the Consensus being molded into a much more rigid model than it once was. Human belief was narrowed drastically to exclude things perceived as &quot;magic,&quot; and to only accept &quot;science and technology.&quot; Revised pushed it even further by specifically saying that the Technocracy screwed up by pushing this narrative <i>too</i> hard, therefore calcifying the Consensus too much and making Paradox even worse.<br /> <br /> <b>Everything</b> was possible before the Order of Reason took charge, with pretty much no consequence. It wasn't a time when magick ruled and technology blew up from Paradox, because <i>Paradox didn't exist.</i> The Consensus was broad enough to encompass primitive technology as well as mystical beliefs just fine. No one got smacked by the Consensus. And then the Technocracy happened. Hell, they invented their own stumbling block, since Paradox doesn't even allow them do some of their more fantastic Effects without a bit of backlash. If they hadn't pushed the narrative so hard of what exactly is possible, there would be so much more they could.<br /> <br /> Now move the idea forward to modern day. The Order of Hermes is filled with plenty on non-Awakened, be they sorcerers or consors, and yet they exist just fine together. House Thig even loves modern tech and uses it extensively in their spells and rituals. Even within their Sanctums, where consors and other non-Awakened reinforce the Hermetic paradigm, thus making their effects easier and more coincidental, their tech <i>works just fine</i>, because they aren't actively disbelieving in it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T18:01:45-07:00","id":983650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/981041-format-space-for-hermetics?p=983635#post983635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do they? Do they really? The Traditions are emphatically not about Mass Ascension. That's the Union's thing. Ascension is personal to the Traditions. I<br /> <br /> And that whole &quot;Let's show the Sleepers the WONDER of magic..&quot; that's just as theoretical a goal as has been previously discussed. That may be a party line. But in practice what do Mage characters actually DO? In most chronicles I've run, played in, read about in the context of Mage in the rules or in the fiction or heard described, the number of games that are about &quot;winning hearts and souls&quot; are in the VAST minority. It's a lot like role-playing running a preschool. You've got to have a GREAT hook to make it interesting at all and an even better one for long term or it's about as interesting as &quot;Mage: the Tax Audit&quot; or &quot;Mage: the Bakery&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ehhh, I don't know. Only the Virtual Adepts really care about Mass Ascension, and they're ex-Technocrats anyway. If there's anything that can be pointed towards as the unifying goal of the Traditions, if they have one, is to allow everyone the freedom to define their own reality. The moral dilemma is how dangerous that might be. On the flip side, while the Technocracy might say that they want to lead humanity to Mass Ascension, it's going to be in their rigid definition, so their moral dilemma is what must be sacrificed to get us there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T00:49:23-07:00","id":983814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/981041-format-space-for-hermetics?p=983635#post983635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they? Do they really? The Traditions are emphatically not about Mass Ascension. That's the Union's thing. Ascension is personal to the Traditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least that's the Tradition's somewhat 'feel better' partyline in order to make members think there's a goal to that whole Ascension War thing <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> It keeps them from remembering that without the Technocracy, they'd probably fall apart in the first place.<br /> <br /> I agree with FrozenFishy that most Tradition Mages simply want to practice their Magick in peace, and that's it.<br /> But that makes a '<i>Let's toss everything back to the Dark Ages</i>' scenario even more weird. Most Mages want to do Magick in peace, and suddenly tossing their whole modern life they grew up in into back to that age is anything but peaceful or comforting.<br /> Most of them not REALLY caring for Mass Ascension even *more* drives the point home that they are not anti-technology, just pro leave-me-alone-Technoracy-thx.<br /> <br /> Last but not least, even if Mass Ascension isn't a thing that most Mages individually strive for...I bet a lot of Mages still have the silent urge to run to a Sleeper and go '<i>Hey, look what we can do!</i>' in that certain, simplistic and honest '<i>Oh my god, if people only knew! If they only knew!</i>' kind of thinking than any bigger motives. It's that frustration Status Quo.<br /> <br /> Also, really..I think it does not come up more in RP because it isn't one of the more exciting kinds of RP for, well, an RPer. I think a Mage, if they were real, would have quite a different amount of investment in the fact.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T08:17:22-07:00","id":983929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/981041-format-space-for-hermetics?p=983641#post983641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even in Revised, that's how it worked. Paradox didn't exist before the Order of Reason got together and started their campaign to win hearts and minds and spread disbelief and doubt in everything that wasn't supported by the Order of Reason. It's specifically called out as a recent phenomena, and it wasn't like there was an absence of primitive technology that didn't work jsut because some of the more mystical arts were still around.<br /> <br /> Paradox is a symptom of the Consensus being molded into a much more rigid model than it once was. Human belief was narrowed drastically to exclude things perceived as &quot;magic,&quot; and to only accept &quot;science and technology.&quot; Revised pushed it even further by specifically saying that the Technocracy screwed up by pushing this narrative <i>too</i> hard, therefore calcifying the Consensus too much and making Paradox even worse.<br /> <br /> <b>Everything</b> was possible before the Order of Reason took charge, with pretty much no consequence. It wasn't a time when magick ruled and technology blew up from Paradox, because <i>Paradox didn't exist.</i> The Consensus was broad enough to encompass primitive technology as well as mystical beliefs just fine. No one got smacked by the Consensus. And then the Technocracy happened. Hell, they invented their own stumbling block, since Paradox doesn't even allow them do some of their more fantastic Effects without a bit of backlash. If they hadn't pushed the narrative so hard of what exactly is possible, there would be so much more they could.<br /> <br /> Now move the idea forward to modern day. The Order of Hermes is filled with plenty on non-Awakened, be they sorcerers or consors, and yet they exist just fine together. House Thig even loves modern tech and uses it extensively in their spells and rituals. Even within their Sanctums, where consors and other non-Awakened reinforce the Hermetic paradigm, thus making their effects easier and more coincidental, their tech <i>works just fine</i>, because they aren't actively disbelieving in it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You are fundamentally misunderstanding my position. It's not that technology will suddenly get paradoxed to death. It's that Science and Reason, the basis for technology working for sleepers, would be shattered. That absolute faith in science and reason that the majority of people hold? That's how Technology for the masses <i>works.</i> That's why every cell phone, every handgun. Every EVERYTHING that isn't a wonder doesn't fall apart or break or just not work.<br /> <br /> If you break that faith, Technology is going to be a casualty to that. People are going to stop believing that the laws of physics and guys in white coats know what they're talking about. The first casualty is going to be the cutting edge stuff. As that faith is shattered, the new technologies are going to stop coming out. The steady upgrades and so on. From there it's a slow downhill decline until you're looking at something like the 40k universe where all the best tech is millenia old and noone knows how to make it anymore.<br /> <br /> And no, Paradox still existed back then, it was just called the Scourge and only really smacked you if you tried something huge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T09:38:13-07:00","id":983949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/981041-format-space-for-hermetics?p=983814#post983814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, really..I think it does not come up more in RP because it isn't one of the more exciting kinds of RP for, well, an RPer. I think a Mage, if they were real, would have quite a different amount of investment in the fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really doubt it. If you could do amazing things, effectively almost ANYTHING, but the price was that you had to keep it secret or else it would hurt you, most mages, like most people, would accept the price-tags that come along with the very very shiny package. <br /> <br /> Knowing that it could work even BETTER if you were willing to not do what you want to do with your amazingness but, instead, to dedicate yourself to an almost certainly fruitless and undoubtedly thankless life, and, to boot, you would specifically go out and hurt yourself a lot more than you would have to otherwise by going out doing the &quot;keep it secret thing&quot;.. No, I really don't think most mages would be evangelist/martyrs. Sure, some of them would be, but most? Probably not. That's a VERY particular type of person, and, even if that particular pathology is more common among mage-types, it probably still wouldn't dominate or even be proportionally large. It simply goes against &quot;avoid pain/seek pleasure&quot; cost-benefit analysis that underlies most subconscious thought processes.<br /> <br /> Sure, the Union does that sort of thing, but look at the elaborate set of cut-outs they go through to minimize the costs and maximize the gains. And the fact that they have institutionalized the whole process. And, even then, most Technocrats are going to act just like other mages most of the time, their protests to the contrary not withstanding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T21:33:15-07:00","id":984234,"title":"","content":"While modern technology does seem to be built on the Consensus, you don't need to <i>totally dissolve</i> the Consensus to just... make modern medicine and faith healing both work. The Alexandrian Society has a coherent paradigm. House Thig has a coherent paradigm. The Ghost Wheel society has a coherent paradigm. The Virtual Adepts have a coherent paradigm. All of those paradigms, moreover, allow modern technology to work <i>just fine</i>. You can have elements of Traditionalist paradigms in the Consensus without <i>completely breaking</i> the scientific advancement process - you just need to still have Awakened around who can pioneer things and develop ideas beyond the cutting edge to expand what the Sleepers can do.<br /> <br /> This worked <i>just fine</i> in the Order of Reason's day, and they didn't have authoritarian hegemony over all First World society. The Enlightened Science -&gt; Extraordinary Science -&gt; Ordinary Science process may work somewhat better with focused, centralized distribution, but it doesn't require strict paradigmatic control.<br /> <br /> Now, can you have <i>all</i> elements of <i>all</i> Traditions paradigms in the Consensus without it breaking down and failing to cohere enough to support Sleepertech? I'd argue no. But expanding the horizons a bit beyond the technodigm isn't an inevitable death knell for modern conveniences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T01:59:54-07:00","id":984315,"title":"","content":"Edit: Never mind. I'm done arguing. I still think Enginseer is wrong, but we're only going in circles now. It's enough to say that I more or less agree with Quantumboost's post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6384,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","user":"Frozenfishy","date":". 10-09-2016, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}